   108→  - _ulid: 01KEZCJPHZ0NV4QECZ6ADZDX1Z
   109→    slugs:
   110→      - ulid-system
   111→      - canonical-ids
   112→    title: ULID Identifier System
   113→    type: feature
   114→    status:
   115→      maturity: draft
   116→      implementation: implemented
   117→    priority: high
   118→    tags:
   119→      - mvp
   120→      - core
   121→    description: |
   122→      ULIDs (Universally Unique Lexicographically Sortable Identifiers)
   123→      serve as the canonical, immutable identifier for every item.
   124→      They are time-sortable, globally unique, and can be shortened
   125→      for display like git commit hashes.
   126→    acceptance_criteria:
   127→      - id: ac-ulid-1
   128→        given: a new item is created
   129→        when: no ULID is provided
   130→        then: a ULID is auto-generated
   131→      - id: ac-ulid-2
   132→        given: a ULID "01KEZCJPHZ86X9PA509GREWDM0"
   133→        when: it needs to be displayed briefly
   134→        then: it can be shortened to "01JHNK" (first 6+ chars)
   135→      - id: ac-ulid-3
   136→        given: an item's ULID
   137→        when: the item is modified
   138→        then: the ULID never changes
   139→    requirements:
   140→      - _ulid: 01KEZCJPHZH6VQH44813GV3PTC
   141→        slugs:
   142→          - ulid-format
   143→        title: ULID Format
   144→        type: requirement
   145→        status:
   146→          maturity: draft
   147→          implementation: implemented
   148→        description: |
   149→          ULIDs are 26-character strings in Crockford base32 encoding.
   150→          Format: TTTTTTTTTTNNNNNNNNNNNNNNNN
   151→          - First 10 chars: Timestamp (millisecond precision)
   152→          - Last 16 chars: Random component
   153→
   154→          Example: 01KEZCJPHZ86X9PA509GREWDM0
   155→        implements:
   156→          - '@ulid-system'
   157→      - _ulid: 01KEZCJPJ0MZSX946EF3ZPW9TA
   158→        slugs:
   159→          - ulid-immutability
   160→        title: ULID Immutability
   161→        type: requirement
   162→        status:
   163→          maturity: draft
   164→          implementation: implemented
   165→        description: |
   166→          Once assigned, a ULID is NEVER changed and NEVER reused.
   167→          If an item is deprecated, its ULID remains; a superseding
   168→          item gets a new ULID and links via supersedes relationship.
   169→        implements:
   170→          - '@ulid-system'
   171→      - _ulid: 01KEZCJPJ0W8V4JZRYZFX56DX5
   172→        slugs:
   173→          - ulid-shortening
   174→        title: ULID Shortening
   175→        type: requirement
   176→        status:
   177→          maturity: draft
   178→          implementation: not_started
   179→        description: |
   180→          ULIDs can be shortened for display and references, similar
   181→          to git commit short hashes. The system resolves short ULIDs
   182→          to full ULIDs, erroring if ambiguous.
   183→
   184→          Minimum recommended: 6 characters
   185→          Full length: 26 characters
   186→        implements:
   187→          - '@ulid-system'
   188→  - _ulid: 01KEZCJPJ0K5S6G1QMBXEVC54W
