   213→        when: either slug is used as a reference
   214→        then: both resolve to the same item
   215→      - id: ac-slug-3
   216→        given: a slug "old-name" assigned to an item
   217→        when: the slug is changed to "new-name"
   218→        then: references to "@old-name" produce a warning but still resolve
   219→    requirements:
   220→      - _ulid: 01KEZCJPJ05XAAVB7JK0G169DP
   221→        slugs:
   222→          - slug-format
   223→        title: Slug Format
   224→        type: requirement
   225→        status:
   226→          maturity: draft
   227→          implementation: implemented
   228→        description: |
   229→          Slugs MUST be lowercase, alphanumeric, with hyphens allowed.
   230→          Pattern: ^[a-z][a-z0-9-]*$
   231→
   232→          Examples: auth-login, user-model, impl-session-v2
   233→        implements:
   234→          - '@slug-system'
   235→      - _ulid: 01KEZCJPJ1HD0JRARXD5AY3ZAW
   236→        slugs:
   237→          - slug-uniqueness
   238→        title: Slug Uniqueness
   239→        type: requirement
   240→        status:
   241→          maturity: draft
   242→          implementation: implemented
   243→        description: |-
   244→          Each slug MUST be unique within the spec. Two items cannot have the same slug.
   245→
   246→          Enforcement:
   247→          - Validation: kspec validate reports duplicate slug errors
   248→          - Prevention: CLI commands reject duplicate slugs at creation/update time
   249→        implements:
   250→          - '@slug-system'
   251→        acceptance_criteria:
   252→          - id: ac-1
   253→            given: a slug 'auth-login' exists in the spec
   254→            when: validation runs
   255→            then: duplicate slug error is reported if another item also has 'auth-login'
   256→          - id: ac-2
   257→            given: a slug 'auth-login' exists in the spec
   258→            when: kspec item add --slug auth-login is run
   259→            then: command fails with 'slug already exists' error
   260→          - id: ac-3
   261→            given: a slug 'auth-login' exists in the spec
   262→            when: kspec item set @other --slug auth-login is run
   263→            then: command fails with 'slug already exists' error
   264→          - id: ac-4
   265→            given: a slug 'auth-login' exists in the spec
   266→            when: kspec task add --slug auth-login is run
   267→            then: command fails with 'slug already exists' error
   268→          - id: ac-5
   269→            given: a slug 'auth-login' exists in the spec
   270→            when: kspec task set @other --slug auth-login is run
   271→            then: command fails with 'slug already exists' error
   272→      - _ulid: 01KEZCJPJ1RC6G58T2XJCJZWB8
   273→        slugs:
   274→          - slug-resolution
   275→        title: Slug Resolution
   276→        type: requirement
   277→        status:
   278→          maturity: draft
   279→          implementation: implemented
   280→        description: |
   281→          When a reference like "@auth-login" is encountered:
   282→          1. Check if it matches a slug exactly
   283→          2. If not found, check if it's a ULID prefix
   284→          3. If still not found, report broken reference error
   285→          4. If ambiguous (multiple matches), report ambiguity error
   286→        implements:
   287→          - '@slug-system'
   288→        acceptance_criteria:
   289→          - id: ac-1
   290→            given: a new item is created with slug 'my-feature'
   291→            when: '@my-feature is referenced immediately after creation'
   292→            then: reference resolves to the newly created item without requiring reload
   293→          - id: ac-2
   294→            given: an item exists with slug 'auth-login'
   295→            when: '@auth-login is referenced'
   296→            then: reference resolves to that item
   297→          - id: ac-3
   298→            given: no item exists with slug 'nonexistent'
   299→            when: '@nonexistent is referenced'
   300→            then: broken reference error is reported
   301→          - id: ac-4
   302→            given: multiple items share ULID prefix '01KEZ'
   303→            when: '@01KEZ is referenced'
   304→            then: ambiguity error is reported listing matching items
